# Queue ownership is queue.ts-local and machine-native: queue-machine.ts is untouched. Each
# mutation attempt captures an owner (composer instance, connection, media lease) and aborts
# through the machine's own AbortController on owner break; the signal is never wired to an HTTP
# call, so an owner break cannot cancel a remote prompt. Publish-side owner checks gate every
# await boundary; prompt admissions re-check through the client's native `prepare` hook.
#
# state.ts attributes legacy media refs at decode ONLY for uniquely scoped (per-draft) containers;
# session-prompt composers share a directory-keyed container and stay unattributed — that residual
# is fenced by the request.ts wire floor and such drafts remain editable. Fork/revert gain only
# the provenance threading; lifecycle guards belong to their upstream machines (#196).
